## 4. Data-display invariants (apply to every number rendered)

- **Colour + arrow + sign always agree**: positive → `var(--up)` + ▲ + `+`; negative → `var(--down)` + ▼ + `−`; zero → `var(--neutral)`, no arrow, `0.00%`.
- **Zero is defined rounding-aware**: if `|pct| < 0.005`, treat as exactly 0. Never render `-0.00%` or `+0.00%`, never colour it, and never include it in gainers/losers rankings.
- All data is **end-of-day**. Never imply live figures. The freshness label `Data as of [date] · end-of-day close, not live` (mono) must always be discoverable near market data.
- Only metrics computable from raw MSE/SECNet scrapes + our stored history may be displayed. If it can't be computed, don't show it.
- Reserve fixed dimensions for every async value (sparklines, charts, ad slots) — CLS ≈ 0.
